.TH FL-BLUETOOTH 1 "November 2026" "fldesktop 0.1.0" "fldesktop"
.SH NAME
fl-bluetooth \- Bluetooth settings for fldesktop
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBfl-bluetooth\fR
.SH DESCRIPTION
Turns Bluetooth on and off, makes the computer visible to other devices,
lists paired devices with their state and battery level, searches for
nearby devices while the window is open, and pairs, connects, disconnects,
trusts and forgets devices. It talks to BlueZ (\fBbluetoothd\fR(8)) and lifts
an rfkill soft block when Bluetooth is turned on.
.PP
Pairing questions (PIN, passkey confirmation, authorization) are asked by
the pairing agent that \fBfl-panel\fR(1) runs for the whole session, and by
fl-bluetooth itself while it is open. The panel's Bluetooth button shows the
state, connects paired devices with one click and announces connected and
disconnected devices as notifications.
.PP
The same view is the Bluetooth page of \fBfl-settings\fR(1).
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
\fBFLD_BLUEZ_BUS\fR=session
Talk to a BlueZ on the session bus (for tests with python-dbusmock).
.SH SEE ALSO
\fBbluetoothctl\fR(1), \fBbluetoothd\fR(8), \fBrfkill\fR(8)
